# synth/synth.ys
#
# Generic (technology-agnostic) Yosys synthesis of rtl/neuron_chip.sv --
# the ASIC-oriented top level (see rtl/neuron_chip.sv's header) -- and its
# real functional-unit hierarchy (register file, ALU, MAC, matrix engine,
# matrix register file, status register, decode, the fetch/decode/execute
# control unit). No simulation-only infrastructure (testbenches, sim/,
# tb/, memory.sv's/memory_sync.sv's $readmemh loader) is part of this
# target -- see docs/MEMORY_INTERFACE.md and asic/README.md for why the
# memory bus is left as chip pins here rather than an internal SRAM model.
#
# This proves the design PARSES, ELABORATES, and SYNTHESIZES cleanly --
# `check` (run both before and after synth) reports multi-driver nets,
# combinational loops, and undriven signals -- and reports cell/register/
# memory statistics via `stat`. It does NOT target a specific standard-
# cell library or PDK (none is committed to this repo -- see
# asic/README.md), so the resulting netlist/statistics are a
# synthesizability proof and a generic-logic area estimate, not a tapeout
# artifact and not a timing signoff. Run via scripts/synth_check.sh, which
# sets the working directory (repo root) and creates build/reports/ this
# script writes into.
#
# Input is not the raw rtl/*.sv files: Yosys's built-in SystemVerilog
# frontend can't parse unpacked-array ports (register_file's regs_dbg,
# the matrix engine/regfile's 4x4 tile ports), so scripts/synth_check.sh
# first runs the RTL through sv2v (https://github.com/zachjs/sv2v) with
# -DSYNTHESIS and --top=neuron_chip, and this script reads that single
# converted Verilog file. `-DSYNTHESIS` matches the `` `ifndef SYNTHESIS ``
# guards around simulation-only code (assertions, $readmemh loaders).

read_verilog build/reports/neuron_chip.sv2v.v

# Elaborate with neuron_chip as top; -check fails the run on an undriven
# or multiply-driven port at the hierarchy level, and on unresolved
# submodule references (a real MODMISSING-equivalent for synthesis).
hierarchy -check -top neuron_chip

# Canonicalize processes (always_comb/always_ff -> RTLIL processes), then
# a first structural check on the design as elaborated, before synthesis
# has touched anything.
proc
check

# Generic technology-independent synthesis: maps always_comb/always_ff
# processes down to generic gates/flops and flattens the hierarchy for a
# single combined statistics report. No target cell library is selected,
# so the cell-count/area numbers below are against Yosys's generic gate
# library ("generic logic"), not a real process's standard cells.
synth -top neuron_chip

# Post-synthesis structural check: catches multiple drivers, undriven
# nets, and combinational loops in the synthesized netlist.
check

stat -top neuron_chip

write_verilog -noattr build/reports/neuron_chip.synth.v
write_json build/reports/neuron_chip.synth.json
